Leave the relcache init file alone in the redo worker.

Redoing a catalog heap record that carries committed invalidation
messages reaches RelationCacheInitFilePreInvalidate, which unlinks the
relcache init file of the database and of global. The redo worker has no
data directory to unlink anything in, and unlink is not on its seccomp
allowlist, so the kernel killed it there and the page service reported
the worker's EOF as a failed batch read.

Caught on server3 reading a project back out of the store, on a cold
attach where pg_class page 0 had to be materialized rather than found in
the local cache. The worker died on every retry, so the project never
came up:

    zou redo: sandbox blocked syscall 87, worker exiting
    postgres(unlink+0xb)
    postgres(RelationCacheInitFilePreInvalidate+0x9c)
    postgres(ProcessCommittedInvalidationMessages+0xe3)
    postgres(heap_redo+0x20b)
    postgres(ZouRedoMain+0x732)
    ERROR zou_pg: getpage 1663/5/1259.0: redo worker failed
    FATAL: zou smgr readv failed with -1 on rel 1259 fork 0

Skipped rather than allowlisted, because there is no init file here and
allowing unlink in the sandbox would let a redo routine delete a file
somebody cares about. The post half is skipped too, since the lock the
pre half takes is the lock it releases.

diff --git a/src/backend/utils/cache/relcache.c b/src/backend/utils/cache/relcache.c
index 559ba9c..c7d9c49 100644
--- a/src/backend/utils/cache/relcache.c
+++ b/src/backend/utils/cache/relcache.c
@@ -39,6 +39,7 @@
 #include "access/tableam.h"
 #include "access/tupdesc_details.h"
 #include "access/xact.h"
+#include "access/zou_walredo.h"
 #include "catalog/binary_upgrade.h"
 #include "catalog/catalog.h"
 #include "catalog/indexing.h"
@@ -6862,6 +6863,17 @@ RelationCacheInitFilePreInvalidate(void)
 	char		localinitfname[MAXPGPATH];
 	char		sharedinitfname[MAXPGPATH];
 
+	/*
+	 * The zou redo worker has no data directory and no relcache init file to
+	 * make obsolete, and unlink() is not on its seccomp allowlist, so the
+	 * kernel kills it here rather than letting it find that out.  Redoing a
+	 * catalog heap record with committed invalidation messages on it reaches
+	 * this function through ProcessCommittedInvalidationMessages, so this is
+	 * every catalog page a tenant reads back out of the store.
+	 */
+	if (zou_redo_active)
+		return;
+
 	if (DatabasePath)
 		snprintf(localinitfname, sizeof(localinitfname), "%s/%s",
 				 DatabasePath, RELCACHE_INIT_FILENAME);
@@ -6884,6 +6896,10 @@ RelationCacheInitFilePreInvalidate(void)
 void
 RelationCacheInitFilePostInvalidate(void)
 {
+	/* The redo worker never took the lock, see above. */
+	if (zou_redo_active)
+		return;
+
 	LWLockRelease(RelCacheInitLock);
 }
 
